    "summary": "AKT1 (RAC-alpha serine/threonine-protein kinase) is the central hub kinase identified by co-expression network analysis of triple-negative breast cancer. Its 3D structure was predicted with AlphaFold2 (ColabFold, MMseqs2 MSA) and characterised with custom Python routines for per-residue confidence, backbone dihedral geometry and Cα contact topology.",
    "pipeline": [
      "FASTA (UniProt P31749)",
      "ColabFold MMseqs2 MSA",
      "AlphaFold2 structure module (5 models)",
      "Top-ranked PDB",
      "pLDDT · PAE · Ramachandran · Contact map"
    ],
    "metrics": [
